IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc22-nunavut`

-- ccc22-tests-nunavut.l4 -- tests for ccc22-nunavut.l4 (sections 573 to 573.2). Every expected value is written from the text, beside the assertion. Arguments are in the order of each function's GIVEN lines.

§ `Section 573 -- Nunavut Court of Justice`

-- (1): args: the person acting is a judge of the NCJ, the holder the Act gives the power to.
#ASSERT `s 573(1) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may exercise the power or perform the duty or function` TRUE `s 573(1) a court of criminal jurisdiction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573(1) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may exercise the power or perform the duty or function` TRUE `s 573(1) a summary conviction court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573(1) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may exercise the power or perform the duty or function` TRUE `s 573(1) a judge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573(1) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may exercise the power or perform the duty or function` TRUE `s 573(1) a provincial court judge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573(1) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may exercise the power or perform the duty or function` TRUE `s 573(1) a justice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573(1) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may exercise the power or perform the duty or function` TRUE `s 573(1) a justice of the peace` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573(1) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may exercise the power or perform the duty or function` TRUE `s 573(1) some other holder` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not one of the six holders the subsection names
#ASSERT `s 573(1) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may exercise the power or perform the duty or function` FALSE `s 573(1) a judge` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the person is not a judge of the NCJ
-- (2): arg: exercised by a judge of the NCJ under (1).
#ASSERT `s 573(2) the power, duty or function is exercised or performed as a judge of a superior court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573(2) the power, duty or function is exercised or performed as a judge of a superior court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): args: presiding at a preliminary inquiry, the remedy is under section 24 of the Charter.
#ASSERT `s 573(3) subsection (2) does not authorize the judge to grant the remedy` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573(3) subsection (2) does not authorize the judge to grant the remedy` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 573(3) subsection (2) does not authorize the judge to grant the remedy` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 573.1 -- Application for review -- Nunavut`

-- (1): args: who applies, the application is to a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut, the decision or order is of a judge of the NCJ, the kind.
#ASSERT `s 573.1(1) an application for review may be made` `s 573.1(1) the Attorney General` TRUE TRUE `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(1) an application for review may be made` `s 573.1(1) the accused` TRUE TRUE `s 573.1(1)(b) relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry, including an order under subsection 548(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(1) an application for review may be made` `s 573.1(1) a person directly affected by the decision or order` TRUE TRUE `s 573.1(1)(c) relating to a subpoena` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(1) an application for review may be made` `s 573.1(1) the accused` TRUE TRUE `s 573.1(1)(d) relating to the publication or broadcasting of information or access to the court room` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(1) an application for review may be made` `s 573.1(1) the accused` TRUE TRUE `s 573.1(1)(e) to refuse to quash an information or indictment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(1) an application for review may be made` `s 573.1(1) the accused` TRUE TRUE `s 573.1(1)(f) relating to the detention, disposal or forfeiture of any thing seized under a warrant or order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(1) an application for review may be made` `s 573.1(1) someone else` TRUE TRUE `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 573.1(1) an application for review may be made` `s 573.1(1) the accused` FALSE TRUE `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not made to a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut
#ASSERT `s 573.1(1) an application for review may be made` `s 573.1(1) the accused` TRUE FALSE `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a decision of a judge of the NCJ
#ASSERT `s 573.1(1) an application for review may be made` `s 573.1(1) the accused` TRUE TRUE `s 573.1(1) some other kind of decision or order` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): args: only a superior court of criminal jurisdiction elsewhere could make it, another statutory right of review is available.
#ASSERT `s 573.1(2) the section bars review of the decision or order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 573.1(2) the section bars review of the decision or order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 573.1(2) the section bars review of the decision or order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) and (2) together: args: answer of (1), answer of (2).
#ASSERT `s 573.1 an application for review may be made, subject to subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 573.1 an application for review may be made, subject to subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1 an application for review may be made, subject to subsection (2)` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): the grounds. args: the kind, the ground, the judge is satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` `s 573.1(1)(d) relating to the publication or broadcasting of information or access to the court room` `s 573.1(3)(a)(i) failed to observe a principle of natural justice or failed or refused to exercise jurisdiction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)(i): any kind
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` `s 573.1(1)(c) relating to a subpoena` `s 573.1(3)(a)(ii) the decision or order was made as a result of an irrelevant consideration or for an improper purpose` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)(ii): any kind
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons` `s 573.1(3)(b)(iv) the warrant is so vague or lacking in particularity that it authorizes an unreasonable search` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) goes with (1)(a)
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` `s 573.1(1)(c) relating to a subpoena` `s 573.1(3)(b)(iv) the warrant is so vague or lacking in particularity that it authorizes an unreasonable search` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) is for a decision mentioned in paragraph (1)(a) only
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` `s 573.1(1)(b) relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry, including an order under subsection 548(1)` `s 573.1(3)(c)(ii) ordered the accused to stand trial when there was no evidence on which a properly instructed jury acting reasonably could convict` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` `s 573.1(1)(b) relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry, including an order under subsection 548(1)` `s 573.1(3)(d) erred in law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (d) is for (1)(c) or (d)
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` `s 573.1(1)(c) relating to a subpoena` `s 573.1(3)(d) erred in law` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` `s 573.1(1)(d) relating to the publication or broadcasting of information or access to the court room` `s 573.1(3)(d) erred in law` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` `s 573.1(1)(e) to refuse to quash an information or indictment` `s 573.1(3)(e)(iii) the provision creating the offence is unconstitutional` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e)
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` `s 573.1(1)(f) relating to the detention, disposal or forfeiture of any thing seized under a warrant or order` `s 573.1(3)(f)(iii) made as a result of reckless disregard for the truth, fraud, intentional misrepresentation or intentional omission` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (f)
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` `s 573.1(1)(e) to refuse to quash an information or indictment` `s 573.1(3)(f)(i) failed to comply with a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (f) is for (1)(f)
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons` `s 573.1(3) none of those grounds` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "only if"
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may grant relief under subsection (4)` `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons` `s 573.1(3)(b)(i) failed to comply with a statutory requirement for the making of the decision or order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied
-- (3), the grounds as a table: args: the kind, the ground. Paragraph (a) lists the grounds for every kind; (b) is for paragraph (1)(a); (c) for (1)(b); (e) for (1)(e).
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the ground is one the subsection names for that kind of decision or order` `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons` `s 573.1(3)(b)(iv) the warrant is so vague or lacking in particularity that it authorizes an unreasonable search` EQUALS TRUE   -- (b)(iv) is a ground for a decision or order relating to a warrant or summons
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the ground is one the subsection names for that kind of decision or order` `s 573.1(1)(c) relating to a subpoena` `s 573.1(3)(b)(iv) the warrant is so vague or lacking in particularity that it authorizes an unreasonable search` EQUALS FALSE   -- the same ground for a subpoena: paragraph (b) is for a decision or order referred to in paragraph (1)(a)
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the ground is one the subsection names for that kind of decision or order` `s 573.1(1)(b) relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry, including an order under subsection 548(1)` `s 573.1(3)(c)(ii) ordered the accused to stand trial when there was no evidence on which a properly instructed jury acting reasonably could convict` EQUALS TRUE   -- (c)(ii) for a decision or order relating to the conduct of a preliminary inquiry
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the ground is one the subsection names for that kind of decision or order` `s 573.1(1)(e) to refuse to quash an information or indictment` `s 573.1(3)(e)(iii) the provision creating the offence is unconstitutional` EQUALS TRUE   -- (e)(iii) for a refusal to quash an information or indictment
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the ground is one the subsection names for that kind of decision or order` `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons` `s 573.1(3)(e)(iii) the provision creating the offence is unconstitutional` EQUALS FALSE   -- (e)(iii) is not a ground for a decision or order relating to a warrant or summons
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the ground is one the subsection names for that kind of decision or order` `s 573.1(1)(c) relating to a subpoena` `s 573.1(3)(a)(i) failed to observe a principle of natural justice or failed or refused to exercise jurisdiction` EQUALS TRUE   -- (a) lists the grounds for every kind named in subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the ground is one the subsection names for that kind of decision or order` `s 573.1(1) some other kind of decision or order` `s 573.1(3)(a)(i) failed to observe a principle of natural justice or failed or refused to exercise jurisdiction` EQUALS FALSE   -- a kind that subsection (1) does not name is outside every paragraph of subsection (3)
#ASSERT `s 573.1(3) the ground is one the subsection names for that kind of decision or order` `s 573.1(1)(a) relating to a warrant or summons` `s 573.1(3) none of those grounds` EQUALS FALSE   -- no ground named in the subsection
-- (4): args: hearing an application for review, what the judge does, the judge's opinion for (f).
#ASSERT `s 573.1(4) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may do this on the hearing of the application` TRUE `s 573.1(4)(a) order a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice to do any act or thing that the judge or any other judge of that court failed or refused to do or has delayed in doing` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(4) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may do this on the hearing of the application` TRUE `s 573.1(4)(b) prohibit or restrain a decision, order or proceeding of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(4) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may do this on the hearing of the application` TRUE `s 573.1(4)(c) declare invalid or unlawful, quash or set aside, in whole or in part, a decision, order or proceeding` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(4) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may do this on the hearing of the application` TRUE `s 573.1(4)(d) refer back for determination in accordance with any directions the judge considers appropriate` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(4) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may do this on the hearing of the application` TRUE `s 573.1(4)(e) grant any remedy under subsection 24(1) of the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(4) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may do this on the hearing of the application` TRUE `s 573.1(4)(f) refuse to grant any relief` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (f) with the opinion
#ASSERT `s 573.1(4) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may do this on the hearing of the application` TRUE `s 573.1(4)(f) refuse to grant any relief` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (f) without the opinion
#ASSERT `s 573.1(4) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may do this on the hearing of the application` TRUE `s 573.1(4)(g) dismiss the application` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(4) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may do this on the hearing of the application` TRUE `s 573.1(4) some other order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 573.1(4) the judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may do this on the hearing of the application` FALSE `s 573.1(4)(g) dismiss the application` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5), (6), (7).
#ASSERT `s 573.1(5) a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may make an interim order pending the final disposition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(5) a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may make an interim order pending the final disposition` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6): args: in the manner directed, within the period, a judge has extended the period.
#ASSERT `s 573.1(6) the application is made as the rules of court direct` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(6) the application is made as the rules of court direct` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- late but extended: "except that a judge ... may at any time extend any period"
#ASSERT `s 573.1(6) the application is made as the rules of court direct` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- late and not extended
#ASSERT `s 573.1(6) the application is made as the rules of court direct` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not in the manner directed
#ASSERT `s 573.1(6) a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may extend the period at any time` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(6) a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut may extend the period at any time` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 573.1(7) an appeal lies to the Court of Appeal of Nunavut and the provisions of Part XXI apply to it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.1(7) an appeal lies to the Court of Appeal of Nunavut and the provisions of Part XXI apply to it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 573.2 -- Habeas corpus`

-- (1): args: in respect of an order or warrant of a judge of the NCJ, (a) only a superior court elsewhere could make it, (b) another statutory right of review or appeal is available.
#ASSERT `s 573.2(1) habeas corpus proceedings may be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.2(1) habeas corpus proceedings may be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "except where (a)"
#ASSERT `s 573.2(1) habeas corpus proceedings may be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "except where (b)"
#ASSERT `s 573.2(1) habeas corpus proceedings may be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): args: with respect to an order or warrant of a judge of the NCJ, brought to challenge the constitutionality of a person's detention or confinement.
#ASSERT `s 573.2(2) habeas corpus proceedings may be brought despite subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.2(2) habeas corpus proceedings may be brought despite subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 573.2(2) habeas corpus proceedings may be brought despite subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) and (2) together: args: answer of (1), answer of (2).
#ASSERT `s 573.2 habeas corpus proceedings may be brought, taking subsections (1) and (2) together` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Despite subsection (1)"
#ASSERT `s 573.2 habeas corpus proceedings may be brought, taking subsections (1) and (2) together` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 573.2 habeas corpus proceedings may be brought, taking subsections (1) and (2) together` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.2(3) subsections 784(2) to (6) apply to the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 573.2(3) subsections 784(2) to (6) apply to the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
